<Base
  title="Terms — JJAY Campus Companion"
  description="The rules for using JJAY Campus Companion: who can sign up, what you may post, and what happens when someone breaks the rules."
>
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="muted small">Effective September 6, 2026</p>

  <div class="card summary">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> be decent to other students. There is no tolerance for
      harassment, hate speech, threats or sexual content — post it and your account goes. Anyone
      can report a message or block a user from inside the app, and reports are reviewed by a
      person. Everything you post is yours; you are responsible for it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    These terms cover JJAY Campus Companion (“the app”), an independent student project. By
    creating an account you agree to them. If you don’t, don’t create one — browsing the app
    doesn’t require an account.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can sign up</h2>
  <p>
    Accounts require a CUNY email address at <code>@login.cuny.edu</code>,
    <code>@jjay.cuny.edu</code>, or <code>@stu-mail.jjay.cuny.edu</code>. You must be at least 13
    years old. One account per person, and the account is yours alone — don’t share it or sign in
    as anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Community guidelines</h2>
  <p>
    These apply to everything you post: chat messages, replies, reactions, GIFs, display names, and
    professor reviews. <strong>There is no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive
    behavior.</strong> Specifically, do not post:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Harassment, bullying, or targeting a specific person.</li>
    <li>Hate speech, or slurs and imagery attacking people for who they are.</li>
    <li>Threats of violence, or anything encouraging self-harm.</li>
    <li>Sexual content, or anything sexualizing a minor.</li>
    <li>Someone else’s private information — address, phone number, schedule, photos.</li>
    <li>Spam, scams, or advertising.</li>
    <li>Impersonating another student, a professor, or college staff.</li>
    <li>Anything illegal, or content you don’t have the right to post.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Professor reviews get one extra rule: write about the class and the teaching. Reviews are not
    a place for personal attacks or claims about a professor’s private life.
  </p>

  <h2>How this is enforced</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatic screening.</strong> Messages and display names are screened before they
      post. Content that clearly breaks these rules is blocked outright.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reporting.</strong> Press and hold any message, or use the report control on a
      review, to report it. Reports are reviewed by a person within 24 hours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Blocking.</strong> You can block any user from the app. You stop seeing their
      messages immediately, and they can’t see yours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consequences.</strong> Content that breaks these rules is removed. Repeat violations
      mute your account temporarily. Serious violations — threats, sexual content involving
      minors, sustained harassment — end the account permanently, without warning.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may remove content or suspend an account at any time to keep the app safe, and we may
    report unlawful content to the appropriate authorities.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    What you post stays yours. By posting it you give us permission to store and display it inside
    the app so other users can see it — nothing more. We don’t sell it, license it to anyone, or
    use it to train anything. Delete your account and it all goes with it; see the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You’re responsible for what you post. Other users’ posts are theirs, not ours — we moderate
    them, but we don’t endorse them, and professor reviews are individual student opinions.
  </p>

  <h2>The app is provided as is</h2>
  <p>
    This is a student project offered free, with no warranty of any kind. Class times, events,
    facility hours and professor data are gathered from public sources and can be wrong or out of
    date — check with the college before relying on any of it. To the extent the law allows, we
    aren’t liable for losses arising from your use of the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account at any time from the Profile tab, and it takes everything with it.
    We can suspend or end an account that breaks these rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change, the new version is posted here with a new effective date. Continuing to
    use the app after that means you accept the change.
  </p>

  <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>
    JJAY Campus Companion is an independent student project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
    by, or sponsored by John Jay College of Criminal Justice or The City University of New York.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms, or to report something urgent:
    <a href="mailto:support@jjayapp.com">support@jjayapp.com</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

